Z||000006||beer_stud_21||11-20-2001||05:48 PM||||blinker-non-usage is so prolific here that the radio DJ's remind people every day.  Doesn't work though.  Nobody uses them.  The thing that gets me the most is people who dont signal or signal right before they turn.  Or worse yet, leave thier signal on and don't turn.  Thats fuggin dangerous!  But it pisses me off when I'm waiting from some shmoe before I pull out and then he turns and I miss my chance and have to wait for some considerate person to let me in to traffic.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>-Marlin<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000007||Nashco||11-20-2001||06:52 PM||||I've found that blinker usage seems to be the worst with people that live in low populated areas, especially noticable when farm-kid moves to the big city!  I have spent a fair amount of time in farm country Ohio, and they don't seem to have any idea what the blinkers are.  My theory is that since normally there's never any cars around anyway, they don't think about it....so when they should use it they "forget" to.<P>Honestly, I don't understand it.  I don't think I've EVER taken a turn, changed lanes, etc. without the signal.  I honestly don't care how people drive around me, as long as I can expect it.  If a person turns their blinker on for three seconds, then I have a chance to back off a few feet...they slide right in front of me, and nobody gets cut off.  I'm very comfortable with driving close to people, as long as I know what to expect.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
