Z||000013||Gold-86SE||11-21-2001||10:21 AM||||<BR>You guys must live in another country or something.  Pleasantville?<P>Down here in Texas, don't you dare indicate you want to move lanes, or you will be cut off.  Down here turn signals are not intended to be to inform other drivers of your intentions, no.  You do your manuver and they change to conform.  Everybody for themself.  <BR>And don't drive the maximum posted speed limit in the left lane or you will be hunted down by all the traffic behind you.  Traffic signage even tells the driver this "Don't slow Texas Down" "Left lane for passing only"<P>But I have found that if I travel in the right hand lane, I can drive faster for greater distances without having to haggle with other drivers.  Most drivers drive in the left and middle lanes (which contradicts what I stated previously but that is the way it is in Texas), which leaves the right open for me.<P>Driving in Texas is totally different than any other state in which I have driven, and I have been in several.  But I would not change it for anything.<P>Oh, and down here, while you are driving through a construction zone, it is not the posted maximum of, let's say, 45mph.  It is 75, 80, and 85.  In New Braunfels, near where I live there is a sign flashing the message "This is not the autobaun"  but we drive 75-85 anyway.  That is Texas drivers.<P>------------------<BR><BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Not So Fair Weather Driver)<BR>84 SE Automatic (Parts Car)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed   (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC Automatic (Blown Engine, seeking 2.5)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed   (Parts Car)||||reg||1
Z||000014||Formula||11-21-2001||10:37 AM||||Gold 86SE - Did you spell texas with a j on purpose? -- tejas -- Just wondering if you made an error or a funny lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||Patrick's Dad||11-21-2001||12:00 PM||||Some of my favorite wifeisms (Things my wife says whether she is a driver or passenger):<P>"Are you waiting for a particular shade of green?"<P>"Nice signal. How 'bout I run you over, *then* beep?"<P>"The sign says 'Yield,' not 'Give Up'."<P>"What are you waiting for, an engraved invitation?"<P>Here in the Boston area, rotarys run counter to the way they run in every other part of the country. The traffic already in the rotary must yield to the traffic entering it.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Gold-86SE||11-21-2001||03:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR><B>Gold 86SE - Did you spell texas with a j on purpose? -- tejas -- Just wondering if you made an error or a funny</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Answer<BR>Texas is the U.S. spelling<BR>Tejas is the Spanish spelling<P>Because of the rich Spanish heritage in Texas, many Texans lovingly refer to Texas as Tejas.<P>When spelled Tejas, it is pronounced like this:<BR>'Te' uses the vowel sound found it 'peg'<BR>'j' is pronounced like 'ha'<BR>'as' used the ending sound of 'moss'<P>so you get something like 'Tehoss'<P>hope this helps.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||JSocha||11-21-2001||04:36 PM||||Hey Gold, I've always wondered about that spelling myself over the years!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> Well, to be totally honest, not really...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> hehehehehe<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000018||avengador1||11-21-2001||05:39 PM||||I don't need people to use their blinkers, I have ESP.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I only signal because I know others out there don't (have ESP/signal your choice). When I signal it doesn't mean that I am asking your permission to change lanes or turn, It means Im going to be doing THAT so WATCH OUT! Don't speed up to try and cut me off because I will run you into the median or of the road for that bonehead stunt. Don't tailgate me after I get in front of you neither because I will go very, very, very, slowwww. I might even slam on my brakes for that invisible dog that just ran in front of me. If you hit me and were tailgating, my neck tends to bruise extremly easy and I will SUE! Thanks for letting me rant a bit. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||avengador1||11-22-2001||11:25 AM||||By the way in Mexico the x has a "J" sound or can be used like one. Texas used to belong to Mexico. They spell the name of their country Mexico not mejico, but it sounds like mejico.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
